{"raw": {"https://jobs.keldair.com/maritime/Faculty/jobs/102740/full-time-tenure-track-humanities-faculty": {"title": "Full-time, Tenure-Track Humanities Faculty", "description": "Careers | Job Application Empty heading Full-time, Tenure-Track Humanities Faculty Buzzards Bay, MA 02532 Posted: 10/14/2026 Deadline: Open until filled Employment: Full-time Pay: $63,000.00 - $68,000.00 per Year Department: Academic Affairs Experience: Intermediate Apply Job Description Division: Academic Affairs; Humanities Division Union Affiliarion: MSCA Supervision Received: Humanities Department Chair and Dean of Undergraduate Studies Supervision Exercised: Subordinate professional, classified, and student personnel in areas of responsibility Massachusetts Maritime Academy invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position as Assistant Professor of Humanities beginning Fall 2027. The position is a 4/4 teaching load that includes teaching core courses (College Writing and Writing About Literature, depending on departmental needs) as well as upper-level courses. General responsibilities: Ability to teach an academic course load of 12 credits per semester (Fall and Spring) within the Humanities Department. These duties will include teaching college writing and the ability to teach writing about literature, depending on departmental needs. Writing Faculty in the Humanities Department teach a wide range of electives \u00a0based on faculty expertise and enrollment. The department\u2019s curriculum may be viewed on the Massachusetts \u00a0Maritime Academy\u2019s website. Massachusetts Maritime Academy is a teaching-focused university, with faculty having many research \u00a0possibilities and publication pathways towards reaching tenure. The selected candidate will be expected to participate in and complement the department\u2019s goals and agendas, including the advancement of General Education throughout the Academy. Faculty are expected to serve as the academic advisors to assigned student advisees and follow all academic procedures and practices of Massachusetts Maritime Academy. All teaching positions at the Massachusetts Maritime Academy require an understanding of the Academy's unique mission and regimental structure. Qualifications and Requirements A Ph.D. in Composition and Rhetoric, Technical or Professional Communication, and/or Writing Studies by Fall 2027. Experience teaching College Writing and the flexibility to teach first-year Writing about Literature. The Humanities Department values principles that foster community, broad representations of experiences and worldviews and will prioritize applications that directly incorporate these values into teaching, research, and service. We seek empathetic teachers, innovative scholars, and collaborative colleagues. We especially \u00a0encourage candidates with skilled student-centric classroom design to apply. Successful candidates will be \u00a0outstanding teachers and active contributors to the department, college, and local community. Demonstrated potential to fulfill evaluation criteria of teaching, service, and advising at the university level Academic rank of the successful candidate determined by licensure, academic background and experience. Preferred Qualifications: We are particularly seeking to hire a colleague with demonstrated interests in pedagogies that are democratic, engage with various local and global communities and their respective needs in our current society, and \u00a0understand the lived experiences of varied embodiments in the classroom. Applicants should also demonstrate \u00a0these commitments in their application materials. Secondary learning environments or experience with students\u2019 transition from high school to college preferred Military, regimental, and/or non-traditional learning environments preferred Preferred candidates will demonstrate experience developing and facilitating curricular goals and/or assessment \u00a0processes. Preferred experience with teaching Technical Writing and/or Business Communications electives. Candidates who can synthesize their research with teaching students with various perspectives, particularly those from non-traditional educational backgrounds, under-represented in higher education, and/or are first generation. Experience teaching in both face-to-face and online modalities. A record of effective teaching appropriate to the applicant\u2019s career stage. Salary: $63,000 - $68,000, based on education, qualifications and experience. Academic rank of the successful candidate determined by licensure, academic background and experience. Company Description Massachusetts Maritime Academy is a top-ranked, fully accredited, four-year, co-educational state university with 7 undergraduate degree programs focusing on science, engineering, technology, math and business that are highly regarded in the domestic and international maritime industry and its related business sectors. Located at the western end of the scenic Cape Cod Canal, MMA is an hour\u2019s drive from the thriving urban communities of Boston, MA and Providence, RI and offers easy access to beautiful Buzzards Bay and the pristine beaches of Cape Cod, Martha\u2019s Vineyard and Nantucket. The Academy offers generous benefits packages and competitive salaries commensurate with qualifications and experience. Benefits Core Benefits Pension Eligible 10 year Vesting (ORP optional) Medical (eight different options) (Pretax) CVS Caremark Prescriptions Dental / Vision Discount through Union or Dept Of Higher Ed Basic Life and AD&D Insurance Paid Family Medical Leave Long Term Disability 403(b) Retirement Plan Smart Plan Deferred Comp Liberal sick and vacation time and paid holidays Free parking Additional Benefits Hinge Health Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA) Dependent Care Accounts (DCA) Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Voluntary Life Insurance AFLAC - Additional Insurance options payroll deduction Metro Credit Union Tuition Reimbursement Please note that benefits are subject to change at any time. Interview Requirements Applicants selected for interview must be prepared to deliver a twenty-minute presentation on a relevant topic provided by MMA. Drug Free, Equal Opportunity Employer, E-Verify Massachusetts Maritime Academy is a drug-free workplace, an Equal Opportunity Employer, and conducts employment verification through E-Verify. Pre-Employment Requirements Offers of employment will be contingent on successfully passing a pre-employment background check and drug screen. Apply Massachusetts Maritime Academy is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer; \u00a0members of under-represented groups are encouraged to apply. Privacy Policy Please ensure Javascript is enabled for purposes of website accessibility"}, "https://jobs.keldair.com/maritime/Faculty/jobs/102729/adjunct-marine-transportation-instructor": {"title": "Adjunct Marine Transportation Instructor", "description": "Careers | Job Application Empty heading Adjunct Marine Transportation Instructor Buzzards Bay, MA 02532 Posted: 10/14/2026 Deadline: Open until filled Employment: Temporary/Contract Pay: Pay is based on the number of credits taught at a rate of $2,343.75/credit Department: Academic Affairs Experience: Other Apply Job Description Division: Academic Affairs General Responsibilities Please note, these are non-benefitted, temporary/contract positions Instruct college-level Marine Transportation courses. Preferred specializations include navigation, ship-handling and shipboard safety, seamanship, and watchstanding. Potential course taught may include Integrated Navigation, Advanced Shiphandling, Coastal Navigation and Electronic Navigation. Massachusetts Maritime Academy follows a \"Learn-Do-Learn\u201d model, where our hands-on simulation labs and classroom experiences enable our students to \"apply\" textbook knowledge in the field. Qualifications and Requirements Hold a Bachelor's Degree in Marine Transportation or related field; Hold a Third Mate license with current Standard of Training, Certification and Watchkeeping (STCW) qualifications. Have at least three years of professional maritime experience Possess an understanding of teaching in the university setting Exhibit excellent oral and written communications skills Understand the unique mission of the university as a maritime academy Preferred Qualifications Holder a master\u2019s degree in Marine Transportation or related field. Have at least three years of maritime experience or teaching experience at an accredited institution of higher learning Salary Pay is based on the number of credits taught at a rate of $2,343.75/credit. The semester credit load is variable, typically between 3 and 11 credits, depending on departmental needs and candidate's expertise. Company Description Massachusetts Maritime Academy is a top-ranked, fully accredited, four-year, co-educational state university with 7 undergraduate degree programs focusing on science, engineering, technology, math and business that are highly regarded in the domestic and international maritime industry and its related business sectors. Located at the western end of the scenic Cape Cod Canal, MMA is an hour\u2019s drive from the thriving urban communities of Boston, MA and Providence, RI and offers easy access to beautiful Buzzards Bay and the pristine beaches of Cape Cod, Martha\u2019s Vineyard and Nantucket. The Academy offers generous benefits packages and competitive salaries commensurate with qualifications and experience. Drug Free, Equal Opportunity Employer, E-Verify Massachusetts Maritime Academy is a drug-free workplace, an Equal Opportunity Employer, and conducts employment verification through E-Verify. Apply Massachusetts Maritime Academy is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer; \u00a0members of under-represented groups are encouraged to apply. Privacy Policy Please ensure Javascript is enabled for purposes of website accessibility"}, "https://jobs.keldair.com/maritime/Faculty/jobs/102724/full-time-tenure-track-natural-science-faculty": {"title": "Full-Time Tenure Track Natural Science Faculty", "description": "Careers | Job Application Empty heading Full-Time Tenure Track Natural Science Faculty Buzzards Bay, MA 02532 Posted: 10/14/2026 Deadline: Open until filled Employment: Full-time Pay: $72,000.00 - $76,000.00 per Year Department: Academic Affairs Experience: Other Apply Job Description Division: Academic Affairs; Science and Mathematics Department Union Affiliarion: MSCA Supervision Received: Reports to the Chair of the Department of Science and Mathematics and to the Vice President of Academic Affairs Supervision Exercised: No supervisory responsibilities General Responsibilities Massachusetts Maritime Academy invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position as Assistant Professor of Natural Sciences beginning Spring 2027 or Fall 2027. The position is a 4/4 teaching load that includes teaching college-level natural science courses (primarily chemistry and biology) from introductory to advanced levels. Candidates must be able to to teach an academic course load of 12 credits per semester (fall and spring) of college-level chemistry and biology courses. Primary teaching responsibilities include introductory chemistry and biology courses including laboratories. Candidates must also be able to teach upper-level chemistry courses including Environmental Chemistry and Organic Chemistry. Ideal candidates will also be capable of teaching physics courses and laboratories. Other job responsibilities include: regular curriculum development and improvement, commitment to professional development, service to the Academy community, participation in the governance process and advising of 10-20 first year students. \u00a0 All teaching positions at the Massachusetts Maritime Academy require computer literacy, excellent written and oral communication skills, and an understanding of the Academy's unique mission. Qualifications and Requirements Hold an earned doctorate in a cross-disciplinary chemistry and biological field; candidates with an earned doctorate in a related field or doctoral candidates with demonstration of progress toward degree will be considered. Demonstrate ability to teach introductory chemistry lectures, biology and laboratory courses. Able to teach developmental and upper college level science courses. Demonstrate commitment to support student learning and to promote student success. Have excellent computer skills and oral and written communication skills. Demonstrate potential to fulfill evaluation criteria for teaching and advising at the college level. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience of at least three years at the post-secondary level. Ability to teach across multiple science disciplines including physics. Understanding of and dedication to the Academy\u2019s unique mission. Experience with assessment of student learning . Experience teaching in both face-to-face and online modalities. Salary $72,000- $76,000 Company Description Massachusetts Maritime Academy is a top-ranked, fully accredited, four-year, co-educational state university with 7 undergraduate degree programs focusing on science, engineering, technology, math and business that are highly regarded in the domestic and international maritime industry and its related business sectors. Located at the western end of the scenic Cape Cod Canal, MMA is an hour\u2019s drive from the thriving urban communities of Boston, MA and Providence, RI and offers easy access to beautiful Buzzards Bay and the pristine beaches of Cape Cod, Martha\u2019s Vineyard and Nantucket. The Academy offers generous benefits packages and competitive salaries commensurate with qualifications and experience. Benefits Core Benefits Pension Eligible 10 year Vesting (ORP optional) Medical (eight different options) (Pretax) CVS Caremark Prescriptions Dental / Vision Discount through Union or Dept Of Higher Ed Basic Life and AD&D Insurance Paid Family Medical Leave Long Term Disability 403(b) Retirement Plan Smart Plan Deferred Comp Liberal sick and vacation time and paid holidays Free parking Additional Benefits Hinge Health Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA) Dependent Care Accounts (DCA) Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Voluntary Life Insurance AFLAC - Additional Insurance options payroll deduction Metro Credit Union Tuition Reimbursement Please note that benefits are subject to change at any time. Interview Requirements Applicants selected for interview must be prepared to deliver a twenty-minute presentation on a relevant topic provided by MMA. Drug Free, Equal Opportunity Employer, E-Verify Massachusetts Maritime Academy is a drug-free workplace, an Equal Opportunity Employer, and conducts employment verification through E-Verify. Pre-Employment Requirements Offers of employment will be contingent on successfully passing a pre-employment background check and drug screen. Apply Massachusetts Maritime Academy is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer; \u00a0members of under-represented groups are encouraged to apply. Privacy Policy Please ensure Javascript is enabled for purposes of website accessibility"}, "https://jobs.keldair.com/maritime/Faculty/jobs/102725/full-time-tenure-track-professional-marine-engineering-faculty": {"title": "Full-time Tenure-Track Professional Marine Engineering Faculty", "description": "Careers | Job Application Empty heading Full-time Tenure-Track Professional Marine Engineering Faculty Buzzards Bay, MA 02532 Posted: 10/14/2026 Deadline: Open until filled Employment: Full-time Pay: $80,000-$84,000, based on education, qualifications, and experience. Department: Academic Affairs Experience: Other Apply Job Description Division: Academic Affairs; Marine Engineering Department Union Affiliarion: MSCA Supervision Received: Reports to the Chair of the Marine Engineering Department and the Associate Dean School of Engineering Supervision Exercised: Subordinate professional, classified, and student personnel in areas of responsibility General Responsibilities The Marine Engineering (ME) Department within the School of Engineering invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position. This position would support the department\u2019s mission to provide high-quality education for students. The successful candidate will be able to teach cadets in a variety of marine engineering-related courses dependent on specialty area. Some areas of instruction include Diesel Propulsion, Machine Tool Technology, Diesel Electric Propulsion Systems, Naval Architecture, High Voltage, Electrical Engineering, Shipboard Engineering Systems (including Steam, Motor, & Gas Turbine), Alternative Fuel Sources, and/or Auxiliary Systems. This full-time faculty member will also advise, mentor, and guide cadets on individual study plans and progress toward degree completion. Additionally, as a member of the Professional Maritime faculty, the selectee will sail aboard the Training Ship in alternating years during a 2-month winter Sea Term and participate in random drug testing. The academic rank of the successful candidate is determined by licensure, educational background, and experience. Qualifications and Requirements A bachelor\u2019s degree in an appropriate field from an institution accredited at the level of such degree A current USCG Second Assistant Unlimited Horsepower with current STCW At least three (3) years of full-time experience in professional service in the maritime field or teaching at an accredited institution of higher learning (or a combination thereof) Understanding of the teaching and advising processes and the application of teaching and advising strategies in the University setting Preferred Qualifications A master\u2019s degree in a related discipline A management level (First/Chief) unlimited horsepower license with current STCW or higher Salary $80,000-$84,000, based on education, qualifications, and experience. Company Description Massachusetts Maritime Academy is a top-ranked, fully accredited, four-year, co-educational state university with 7 undergraduate degree programs focusing on science, engineering, technology, math and business that are highly regarded in the domestic and international maritime industry and its related business sectors. Located at the western end of the scenic Cape Cod Canal, MMA is an hour\u2019s drive from the thriving urban communities of Boston, MA and Providence, RI and offers easy access to beautiful Buzzards Bay and the pristine beaches of Cape Cod, Martha\u2019s Vineyard and Nantucket. The Academy offers generous benefits packages and competitive salaries commensurate with qualifications and experience. Benefits Core Benefits Pension Eligible 10 year Vesting (ORP optional) Medical (eight different options) (Pretax) CVS Caremark Prescriptions Dental / Vision Discount through Union or Dept Of Higher Ed Basic Life and AD&D Insurance Paid Family Medical Leave Long Term Disability 403(b) Retirement Plan Smart Plan Deferred Comp Liberal sick and vacation time and paid holidays Free parking Additional Benefits Hinge Health Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA) Dependent Care Accounts (DCA) Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Voluntary Life Insurance AFLAC - Additional Insurance options payroll deduction Metro Credit Union Tuition Reimbursement Please note that benefits are subject to change at any time. Interview Requirements Applicants selected for interview must be prepared to deliver a twenty-minute presentation on a relevant topic provided by MMA. Drug Free, Equal Opportunity Employer, E-Verify Massachusetts Maritime Academy is a drug-free workplace, an Equal Opportunity Employer, and conducts employment verification through E-Verify. Pre-Employment Health Requirements Offers of employment will be contingent on successfully passing a pre-employment background check, drug screen and physical examination. Apply Massachusetts Maritime Academy is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer; \u00a0members of under-represented groups are encouraged to apply. Privacy Policy Please ensure Javascript is enabled for purposes of website accessibility"}, "https://jobs.keldair.com/maritime/Faculty/jobs/102726/full-time-emergency-management-and-homeland-security-faculty": {"title": "Full-Time Emergency Management & Homeland Security Faculty", "description": "Careers | Job Application Empty heading Full-Time Emergency Management & Homeland Security Faculty Buzzards Bay, MA 02532 Posted: 10/14/2026 Deadline: Open until filled Employment: Full-time Pay: $70,000- $75,000; Academy offers generous benefits and a competitive salary commensurate with education, qualifications and experience. Department: Academic Affairs Experience: Intermediate Apply Job Description Division: Academic Affairs; Emergency Management Division Union Affiliarion: MSCA Supervision Received: Emergency Management Department Chair and Dean of Undergraduate Studies Supervision Exercised: Subordinate professional, classified, and student personnel in areas of responsibility General Responsibilities Ability to teach an academic course load of 12 credits per semester (Fall and Spring) of college-level courses within the Emergency Management Department. Teaching responsibilities would primarily include Emergency Management and Homeland Security topic areas, along with related departmental courses as needed. The department\u2019s curriculum may be viewed on the Massachusetts Maritime Academy\u2019s website. Regular curriculum development and improvement. Participation in various academic committees in support of the Department and Academy. Participation in Emergency Management Department Experiential Learning Programs, teaching and supervising students in an off-campus, residential setting. \u00a0Participation involves traveling and residing away from the faculty member\u2019s domicile. Serving as an academic advisor to assigned student advisees. All teaching positions at the Massachusetts Maritime Academy require computer literacy, excellent written and oral communication skills, and an understanding of the Academy's unique mission. Qualifications and Requirements The Academy is seeking candidates for one full-time faculty position. Based on the qualifications and experience of the selected candidate, the position may be filled as either a tenure-track or non-tenure-track appointment, as follows: Full-Time, Tenure Track Position: For a full-time, tenure-track position, candidates must have a Doctorate in Emergency Management or related field (including public health, public administration or law) by Fall 2027 and be able to teach in one or more of the following areas: Emergency Management Policy, Procedure, and Theory, Environmental/ Occupational Health and Safety, Cybersecurity, Exercise Design and Development, Emergency Planning, Emergency Management Communications, GIS and/or Emergency Management related Information Technology courses, and related subject areas. Full-Time, non-Tenure Track Position: Candidates with a master\u2019s degree and relevant field experience are encouraged to apply and may be considered for a Full-Time Temporary Faculty position for the 2027-2028 Academic Year (September 2027 - June 2028). This is a one-year, benefited, non-tenure-track position with potential for renewal. In addition, all candidates must have the following qualifications: Demonstrated potential to fulfill evaluation criteria for teaching and advising at the college level. Excellent oral and written communication skills, and computer skills. Understanding and appreciation of the Academy's unique mission. Preferred Qualifications Professional licenses/certifications related to Emergency Management (e.g. CEM or AEM), National & Homeland Security, and/ or Environmental/ Occupational Health and Safety Record of relevant academic research and writing Salary $70,000- $75,000; Academy offers generous benefits and a competitive salary commensurate with education, qualifications and experience. Company Description Massachusetts Maritime Academy is a top-ranked, fully accredited, four-year, co-educational state university with 7 undergraduate degree programs focusing on science, engineering, technology, math and business that are highly regarded in the domestic and international maritime industry and its related business sectors. Located at the western end of the scenic Cape Cod Canal, MMA is an hour\u2019s drive from the thriving urban communities of Boston, MA and Providence, RI and offers easy access to beautiful Buzzards Bay and the pristine beaches of Cape Cod, Martha\u2019s Vineyard and Nantucket. The Academy offers generous benefits packages and competitive salaries commensurate with qualifications and experience. Benefits Core Benefits Pension Eligible 10 year Vesting (ORP optional) Medical (eight different options) (Pretax) CVS Caremark Prescriptions Dental / Vision Discount through Union or Dept Of Higher Ed Basic Life and AD&D Insurance Paid Family Medical Leave Long Term Disability 403(b) Retirement Plan Smart Plan Deferred Comp Liberal sick and vacation time and paid holidays Free parking Additional Benefits Hinge Health Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA) Dependent Care Accounts (DCA) Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Voluntary Life Insurance AFLAC - Additional Insurance options payroll deduction Metro Credit Union Tuition Reimbursement Please note that benefits are subject to change at any time. Interview Requirements Applicants selected for interview must be prepared to deliver a twenty-minute presentation on a relevant topic provided by MMA. Drug Free, Equal Opportunity Employer, E-Verify Massachusetts Maritime Academy is a drug-free workplace, an Equal Opportunity Employer, and conducts employment verification through E-Verify. Pre-Employment Requirements Offers of employment will be contingent on successfully passing a pre-employment background check and drug screen. Apply Massachusetts Maritime Academy is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer; \u00a0members of under-represented groups are encouraged to apply. Privacy Policy Please ensure Javascript is enabled for purposes of website accessibility"}}, "rows": {"https://jobs.keldair.com/maritime/Faculty/jobs/102740/full-time-tenure-track-humanities-faculty": {"school_id": 546, "posting_url": "https://jobs.keldair.com/maritime/Faculty/jobs/102740/full-time-tenure-track-humanities-faculty", "job_title_in_post": "Full-time, Tenure-Track Humanities Faculty", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Business Communications electives", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://jobs.keldair.com/maritime/Faculty/jobs/102729/adjunct-marine-transportation-instructor": {"school_id": 546, "posting_url": "https://jobs.keldair.com/maritime/Faculty/jobs/102729/adjunct-marine-transportation-instructor", "job_title_in_post": "Adjunct Marine Transportation Instructor", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Marine Transportation; written communications skills Understand the", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://jobs.keldair.com/maritime/Faculty/jobs/102724/full-time-tenure-track-natural-science-faculty": {"school_id": 546, "posting_url": "https://jobs.keldair.com/maritime/Faculty/jobs/102724/full-time-tenure-track-natural-science-faculty", "job_title_in_post": "Full-Time Tenure Track Natural Science Faculty", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Natural Science; online modalities", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://jobs.keldair.com/maritime/Faculty/jobs/102725/full-time-tenure-track-professional-marine-engineering-faculty": {"school_id": 546, "posting_url": "https://jobs.keldair.com/maritime/Faculty/jobs/102725/full-time-tenure-track-professional-marine-engineering-faculty", "job_title_in_post": "Full-time Tenure-Track Professional Marine Engineering Faculty", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://jobs.keldair.com/maritime/Faculty/jobs/102726/full-time-emergency-management-and-homeland-security-faculty": {"school_id": 546, "posting_url": "https://jobs.keldair.com/maritime/Faculty/jobs/102726/full-time-emergency-management-and-homeland-security-faculty", "job_title_in_post": "Full-Time Emergency Management & Homeland Security Faculty", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Emergency Management & Homeland Security; Emergency Management Policy", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}}, "school_id": 546, "status": "complete", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T18:44:20+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-10-16T18:44:20+00:00", "last_error": ""}